## 2.2 Fairness Constraints (The Anti-Frustration Constitution)

These are **hard-coded behavioral rules** — bots must NEVER violate them:

1. **No aimbot**: Bots must always apply aim error. Even PRO-tier bots have ≥ 3° of intentional aim scatter.
2. **No wallhacks**: Bots may only react to enemies they have "line of sight" to (using simple raycast or distance+angle check). Exception: if enemy fired a loud weapon within 400px in the last 0.5s, bots may "hear" them.
3. **No instant reaction**: Minimum reaction time is **220ms** for lowest tier bots, **110ms** for highest tier. Reaction time includes: detect → decide → act.
4. **No perfect prediction**: Bots predict player movement with **intentional velocity error** (see §15.3).
5. **No damage stacking**: If the player has been hit 3+ times in the last 2 seconds, bots deal 20% reduced damage to the player for the next 1 second (anti-gangbang).
6. **No focus-fire**: Bots must randomize targets. When 3+ bots are within 400px of the player and no other enemy is present, at most 2 bots may target the player at once. The 3rd bot must "distract" (attack a different target or reposition).
7. **Rubber-band for losers**: When player is losing badly (see §6.3), bot aggression AND accuracy are reduced.
8. **Rubber-band for winners**: When player is dominating (see §6.4), bots coordinate more and play better — but never above the tier ceiling.
9. **Kill attribution fairness**: If a bot is about to kill the player, and there is a lootable medkit within 100px, the bot must give the player 1.5s to pick it up before executing. (Grace-period system.)
10. **No spawn kills**: Bots must not attack any entity that has been "alive and landed" for less than 3 seconds.
11. **No storm-luring**: Bots must not intentionally push the player into storm damage. They may use storm strategically for themselves.
12. **Cooldown respect**: Bots use their abilities exactly like the player — same cooldowns, same mana costs, same range limits. No exceptions.
13. **No teleporting**: Bots must obey all the movement physics the player does.

