# 7. BOT AI ARCHITECTURE OVERVIEW

The new bot AI will use a **layered architecture**, with each layer having a specific job:

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  LAYER 1: PERCEPTION (every 100-200ms per bot)      │
│  - Line of sight checks                             │
│  - Sound event processing                           │
│  - Memory update (last known positions)             │
│  - Reaction queue insertion                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  LAYER 2: DECISION (every 100-300ms per bot)        │
│  - Utility scoring (which action has highest value) │
│  - State selection (high-level mode)                │
│  - Target selection (who to focus)                  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  LAYER 3: TACTICS (every frame)                     │
│  - Path calculation (A* or steering)                │
│  - Aim calculation (predictive)                     │
│  - Attack timing (cooldown-aware)                   │
│  - Dodge calculation                                │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  LAYER 4: FAIRNESS OVERRIDE (every frame)           │
│  - Damage caps, reaction floors, rubber-band        │
│  - Showmanship injection                            │
│  - Anti-frustration adjustments                     │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Each layer runs at a different frequency** to save CPU:
- Perception: 5-10 Hz per bot (200-100ms interval)
- Decision: 3-10 Hz per bot (100-300ms interval)
- Tactics: 60 Hz (every frame) — but this is the cheapest layer
- Fairness: 60 Hz (cheap bit flips only)

## 7.1 Update Frequency Table

| Distance from player | Perception Rate | Decision Rate | Tactics |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0-400px | 10 Hz | 10 Hz | 60 Hz |
| 400-800px | 8 Hz | 6 Hz | 60 Hz |
| 800-1500px | 5 Hz | 4 Hz | 60 Hz |
| 1500+ px | 3 Hz | 2 Hz | 30 Hz (interpolated) |

**This LOD system saves 60-80% of AI CPU** compared to running all bots at full rate.

## 7.2 Accumulator-Based Scheduling

Each bot has timers:
```javascript
bot._perceptionTimer = 0;
bot._decisionTimer = 0;

// In game loop (once per frame):
const dt = deltaTime;
bot._perceptionTimer += dt;
if (bot._perceptionTimer >= bot._perceptionInterval) {
    bot._perceptionTimer = 0;
    runPerception(bot);
}
// Same for decision...
```

**Allocation rule**: All interval values are pre-stored on the bot object. No objects created per frame.

