# 10. COMBAT AI DEEP DIVE

This is where the "100x better" really shows.

## 10.1 Predictive Aiming

Instead of aiming at the enemy's current position, aim at where they **will be**:

```javascript
function calculateAimAngle(bot, target, projectileSpeed) {
    // Current relative position
    let dx = target.x - bot.x;
    let dy = target.y - bot.y;
    let dist = Math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy);
    
    // Time for projectile to reach target
    let t = dist / projectileSpeed;
    
    // Predict target position at time t
    // Use target's velocity (player velocity = last frame movement)
    const targetVx = (target.x - target.prevX) / deltaTime;
    const targetVy = (target.y - target.prevY) / deltaTime;
    
    let predictedX = target.x + targetVx * t;
    let predictedY = target.y + targetVy * t;
    
    // Iterate (2 rounds) for accuracy
    for (let i = 0; i < 2; i++) {
        dx = predictedX - bot.x;
        dy = predictedY - bot.y;
        dist = Math.sqrt(dx*dx + dy*dy);
        t = dist / projectileSpeed;
        predictedX = target.x + targetVx * t;
        predictedY = target.y + targetVy * t;
    }
    
    // Add tier-based aim error
    const aimErrorRad = bot.aimError;
    predictedX += (Math.random() - 0.5) * aimErrorRad * dist;
    predictedY += (Math.random() - 0.5) * aimErrorRad * dist;
    
    return Math.atan2(predictedY - bot.y, predictedX - bot.x);
}
```

**Aim error values by tier** (in radians per 100px of distance):

| Tier | Aim Error | Effective hit rate at 300px |
|---|---|---|
| NOOB | 0.15 | ~35% |
| ROOKIE | 0.12 | ~48% |
| AVERAGE | 0.09 | ~62% |
| SKILLED | 0.065 | ~75% |
| VETERAN | 0.045 | ~85% |
| ELITE | 0.03 | ~91% |
| PRO | 0.018 | ~95% |

**The player can dodge even PRO-level bots** because 5% miss rate at 300px is meaningful, and the bot doesn't know where the player will dodge.

## 10.2 Projectile Dodging

When a projectile is inbound, the bot evaluates dodge options:

```javascript
function evaluateDodge(bot, projectile) {
    // Calculate time to impact
    const dx = projectile.x - bot.x;
    const dy = projectile.y - bot.y;
    const pvx = projectile.vx;
    const pvy = projectile.vy;
    const pSpeed = Math.sqrt(pvx*pvx + pvy*pvy);
    
    // Projected closest approach
    const tClosest = -(dx * pvx + dy * pvy) / (pSpeed * pSpeed);
    if (tClosest < 0 || tClosest > 1.5) return null;  // not a threat
    
    const closestX = projectile.x + pvx * tClosest;
    const closestY = projectile.y + pvy * tClosest;
    const missDist = Math.sqrt((closestX - bot.x) ** 2 + (closestY - bot.y) ** 2);
    
    if (missDist > bot.radius + 30) return null;  // won't hit anyway
    
    // Determine perpendicular direction
    const perpAngle = Math.atan2(pvy, pvx) + Math.PI / 2;
    
    // Two dodge options: perpendicular left, perpendicular right
    const dodgeLeftX = bot.x + Math.cos(perpAngle) * 60;
    const dodgeLeftY = bot.y + Math.sin(perpAngle) * 60;
    const dodgeRightX = bot.x - Math.cos(perpAngle) * 60;
    const dodgeRightY = bot.y - Math.sin(perpAngle) * 60;
    
    // Choose the direction that stays safer (closer to storm center, away from enemies, not into walls)
    const leftScore = scoreEscapePosition(bot, dodgeLeftX, dodgeLeftY);
    const rightScore = scoreEscapePosition(bot, dodgeRightX, dodgeRightY);
    
    return leftScore > rightScore ? 'LEFT' : 'RIGHT';
}
```

**Dodge success by tier** (chance bot decides to dodge when it should):

| Tier | Dodge Decision Rate | Dodge Execution Accuracy |
|---|---|---|
| NOOB | 15% | 40% |
| ROOKIE | 30% | 55% |
| AVERAGE | 50% | 70% |
| SKILLED | 70% | 80% |
| VETERAN | 85% | 88% |
| ELITE | 92% | 92% |
| PRO | 97% | 95% |

So a PRO bot successfully dodges ~92% of dodgable projectiles. A NOOB dodges ~6% of them (feels like a beginner).

## 10.3 Attack Timing

Bots use attacks **at optimal times**, not spammingly:

- **Melee**: Use when enemy is in range AND enemy is not invulnerable AND bot's attack is off cooldown. Bot will **pre-position** (approach to melee range) 0.3s before attacking.
- **Spell**: Use when enemy is in range AND (enemy is not dashing AND enemy is not behind cover) AND mana ≥ cost AND cooldown ready. Bot will **lead the target** (predictive aim).
- **Ult**: Use when:
  - Enemy is at low HP (kill-securing) — highest priority
  - Enemy is grouped with another enemy (AoE value) — for BERSERKER/TIDECALLER
  - Enemy is about to attack (defensive use) — for SHADOW dash-ult
  - Bot has been in combat for > 3s (ult is "loaded")
  - Bot's HP is high enough to survive the trade

**Ult usage by tier:**

| Tier | Ult Usage Rate | Ult Timing Quality |
|---|---|---|
| NOOB | 30% (often forgets) | Random |
| ROOKIE | 50% | Random |
| AVERAGE | 70% | Uses on low HP |
| SKILLED | 85% | Uses on low HP + group |
| VETERAN | 92% | Also uses defensively |
| ELITE | 96% | Also uses for zone denial |
| PRO | 99% | Perfect timing |

## 10.4 Melee Combat Positioning

For melee-range bots (BERSERKER, SHADOW):

- **Approach path**: Not straight-line. Approach in a curve (arc) to avoid being led.
- **Commit distance**: When within 2x melee range, commit to the attack (no more repositioning).
- **Attack facing**: Always face the enemy when swinging.
- **Post-attack reposition**: After a melee swing, move in a random perpendicular direction (don't stand still).

## 10.5 Ranged Combat Positioning

For ranged bots (TIDECALLER mainly, SHADOW secondary):

- **Kiting**: Maintain distance of 60-75% of max spell range
- **Strafe**: Continuously strafe left-right to avoid being hit
- **Cover use**: If cover exists nearby, retreat to cover, attack from behind cover
- **Zoning**: Fire spells to deny certain movement paths, not just to hit

## 10.6 Group Combat

When 2+ bots are near each other, they engage in **focus-fire coordination**:

- **Target caller**: The highest-tier bot in the group "calls" the target
- **Focus fire**: All bots in the group attack the same target (within tier-appropriate coordination chance)
- **Pincer**: If possible, bots spread to surround the target
- **Cover fire**: If one bot is reloading (cooldown), another covers its retreat

**Coordination by tier:**
- NOOB-ROOKIE: 0% coordination (each bot is individual)
- AVERAGE: 20% coordination (weak)
- SKILLED: 45% coordination
- VETERAN: 65% coordination
- ELITE: 80% coordination
- PRO: 92% coordination

**Critical fairness rule**: Coordination **never applies to the player alone**. If the only enemy is the player, coordination caps at 40% (see §15).

