# 13. ADVANCED BEHAVIORAL SYSTEMS

These are the systems that create "wow, that bot is smart" moments.

## 13.1 Feint & Bait

High-tier bots can bait the player:

- **Bait retreat**: Bot pretends to retreat, then turns and attacks when player follows
- **Bait dash**: Bot moves in a pattern that suggests it will dash, then doesn't (wastes player's dodge)
- **Bait ult**: Bot moves toward player aggressively, but holds ult (threatens without using)

**This is executed only by ELITE+ bots AND only when player MMR > 500** (so new players don't feel tricked).

## 13.2 Pattern Recognition

Bots track the player's **movement patterns** over the last 3 seconds:

- Does the player prefer to circle left or right?
- Does the player dash when at 40% HP?
- Does the player attack after a spell lands?

Bots use this to **predict** the player's next move and pre-position counterplay.

**This is subtle**: bots don't "read your mind", but they "notice your habits."

**Only PRO-tier bots use this** AND only after the player has been observed for 4+ seconds.

## 13.3 Cooldown Tracking (Player)

Bots track the player's **cooldown state** visually:

- If player cast a spell, bot knows spell is on cooldown for the next 0.8s
- If player dashed, bot knows dash is on cooldown for the next 1.5s
- Bot uses these gaps to attack

**This is fair** — the player can see bots' spells/cooldowns too. Bots track the same info.

## 13.4 Emotional Simulation

Bots have a **morale** value that affects behavior:

- If bot has been losing fights → morale drops → bot plays more cautiously
- If bot has been winning → morale rises → bot plays more aggressively
- Morale resets every 30 seconds

This makes bots feel **alive** — they "get scared" if they've been beaten.

## 13.5 Learning Adaptation

Within a match, each bot **adapts** to the player:

- If player dodges left 3 times, bot starts aiming right
- If player always uses ult at 50% HP, bot pre-emptively attacks at 60% HP
- If player always retreats to cover, bot attacks before player reaches cover

**This learning is per-bot, resets each match, and is capped at moderate strength.** Bots don't become omniscient — they just "learn your tricks."

## 13.6 Last-Stand Behavior

When a bot is the **last bot alive** vs. the player:

- Bot becomes dramatically more aggressive (this is the "boss" moment)
- Bot uses ult more freely
- Bot coordinates with no allies (it's alone)

But: bot's accuracy **decreases by 10%** (adrenaline effect) — this is the "fairness grace" for the final fight.

