# 14. BOT COOPERATION & SOCIAL AI

Bots should feel like they're "on the same team" when facing the player, but not omniscient.

## 14.1 Global Bot Coordination Channel

Bots share limited information:

- `bot.lastKnownPlayerPosition`: shared with other bots within 500px (their voice range)
- `bot.damageEvents`: when a bot damages the player, nearby bots receive a "target info" update
- `bot.engagementStatus`: bots know if an ally is engaged with an enemy

**NOT shared**: exact positions behind walls, cooldown states, etc.

## 14.2 Target Delegation

When 2+ bots are near the player:

- **Anti-overkill**: If 2 bots are already on the player, the 3rd bot attacks a different enemy (if any exists)
- **Flanking**: One bot engages from front, one from side (tier-appropriate)
- **Cover fire**: One bot attacks, one bot suppresses (stays visible but doesn't commit)

## 14.3 Group Strategy

Bots within 400px of each other form an **informal group**:

- Group has a "leader" (highest tier)
- Group has a "formation" (line, wedge, or clustered)
- Group moves and attacks together

**Group size caps at 3 bots** — larger groups are chaotic and unfair.

## 14.4 "Fight Club" Prevention

Two bots don't team up on one target forever. After 8 seconds of engagement:

- The bot with the lowest HP disengages and looks for loot
- Or the bot re-targets a different enemy

This prevents 2 bots from feeling like an unbeatable "duo."

## 14.5 Protection of Low-HP Bots

When a bot is at < 20% HP:

- Other bots in range may "cover" its retreat
- The covering bot turns toward the threat, fires a spell to suppress
- This is capped at 2 seconds per cover event

