# 16. MOBILE PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION LAYER

Every line of AI code must pass a performance review.

## 16.1 Allocation Audit

**Zero allocations in the hot loop.** Every data structure that lives for the match is pre-allocated:

```javascript
// At init:
bot.perception.visibleEnemies.length = 0;  // reused
bot._cachedPath = [];                       // reused array
bot._pathClearTimer = 0;                    // numeric
bot._dodgeCooldown = 0;                     // numeric
```

**No new objects per frame.** If a temporary object is truly needed (rare), it's from a **pool**:

```javascript
const tempVectorPool = [];
for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++) tempVectorPool.push({x: 0, y: 0});
let tempVectorIndex = 0;
function getTempVector() {
    const v = tempVectorPool[tempVectorIndex];
    tempVectorIndex = (tempVectorIndex + 1) % tempVectorPool.length;
    return v;
}
```

## 16.2 Distance Check Optimization

Never use `Math.hypot`. Use squared distance:

```javascript
function distanceSq(ax, ay, bx, by) {
    const dx = bx - ax;
    const dy = by - ay;
    return dx * dx + dy * dy;
}
```

Compare against `maxRange * maxRange` instead of `Math.sqrt`.

## 16.3 Viewport Culling

Bots that are **off-screen** get **reduced update rate**:

```javascript
const isOnScreen = (bot.x > Camera.x - viewHalfW && 
                    bot.x < Camera.x + viewHalfW &&
                    bot.y > Camera.y - viewHalfH &&
                    bot.y < Camera.y + viewHalfH);

bot._updateInterval = isOnScreen ? 0.1 : 0.33;  // 10Hz vs 3Hz
```

**This saves ~60% of AI CPU on a typical match.**

## 16.4 Cached Values

Frequently computed values are cached:

```javascript
bot._perceptionCache = {
    targetAngle: 0,
    targetDistanceSq: 0,
    lastCacheTime: 0,
};

if (game.time - bot._perceptionCache.lastCacheTime > 0.15) {
    // recompute
    bot._perceptionCache.lastCacheTime = game.time;
}
```

## 16.5 Bitmask Flags

Bot state flags use bits, not booleans, to save memory and improve cache locality:

```javascript
bot._flags = 0;
const FLAG_AGGRESSIVE = 1;
const FLAG_RETREATING = 2;
const FLAG_ULT_READY = 4;
const FLAG_DODGING = 8;
// etc.

if (bot._flags & FLAG_ULT_READY) { ... }
```

## 16.6 LOD (Level of Detail) for AI

Far-away bots use **simplified AI**:

```javascript
if (distanceSq(bot, player) > 1500 * 1500) {
    // LOD 2: Very simple AI
    // - No perception checks
    // - No pathfinding
    // - Just wander / flee storm
    // - Full resolution physics still run (visual continuity)
    runSimpleAI(bot, dt);
    return;
} else if (distanceSq(bot, player) > 800 * 800) {
    // LOD 1: Medium AI
    // - Perception at 5Hz
    // - Decision at 3Hz
    // - Simple pathfinding
    runMediumAI(bot, dt);
    return;
} else {
    // LOD 0: Full AI
    runFullAI(bot, dt);
}
```

**LOD saves 70-80% of AI CPU on a full map.**

## 16.7 Budgeted A*

Only N bots can A* per frame:

```javascript
let astarBudget = 3;  // per frame

function requestAstar(bot) {
    if (astarBudget <= 0) {
        bot._astarPending = true;
        return false;
    }
    astarBudget--;
    return true;
}

// In loop:
astarBudget = 3;  // reset each frame
for (each bot) {
    if (bot._needsPath && requestAstar(bot)) {
        bot._cachedPath = findPath(bot);
        bot._needsPath = false;
    }
}
```

## 16.8 No String Concatenation

Never build strings in the loop. If needed for debugging, use `console.log` behind a `DEBUG_AI` flag.

## 16.9 Hoisted Functions

Every function referenced in the hot loop is **hoisted** or **pre-bound**:

```javascript
// Bad:
bots.forEach(b => { b.update(Math.random()); });

// Good:
for (let i = 0; i < bots.length; i++) {
    const b = bots[i];
    b.update(i);
}
```

## 16.10 Profiling Hooks

Include optional profiling (disabled in production):

```javascript
const AI_PROFILING = false;
let aiTimeSamples = [];

if (AI_PROFILING) {
    const t0 = performance.now();
    // ... AI work
    aiTimeSamples.push(performance.now() - t0);
    if (aiTimeSamples.length > 60) {
        const avg = aiTimeSamples.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / aiTimeSamples.length;
        console.log(`AI avg: ${avg.toFixed(2)}ms`);
        aiTimeSamples = [];
    }
}
```

