# 19. TESTING & TUNING PROTOCOLS

## 19.1 Test Scenarios

Before shipping, run through these scenarios:

### Test 1: New Player First Match
- **Setup**: Player MMR = 200 (Beginner), Match 1
- **Expected**: Player kills 3-5 bots, places top 3, wins or nearly wins
- **Bots should**: Miss often, retreat when attacked, dodge rarely, forget the player quickly
- **Time to complete**: 8-12 minutes
- **Feel**: "I'm pretty good at this game"

### Test 2: Skilled Player Mid-Game
- **Setup**: Player MMR = 550 (Advanced), Match 10
- **Expected**: Player wins 40% of matches, dies to coordinated bots
- **Bots should**: Land spells, dodge some, flank, use ults
- **Time to complete**: 6-10 minutes
- **Feel**: "These bots are actually good"

### Test 3: Struggling Player
- **Setup**: Player on losing streak (3+ losses), MMR = 300
- **Expected**: Player wins 60% of matches
- **Bots should**: Play worse than usual, miss more, retreat more
- **Time to complete**: 8-12 minutes
- **Feel**: "I got my groove back"

### Test 4: Late Game
- **Setup**: 3 bots remain, player has 60% HP
- **Expected**: Bots coordinate, challenge player, but player can win
- **Bots should**: Flank, cover-fire, use ults defensively
- **Feel**: "This is an epic final fight"

### Test 5: Low-End Mobile Performance
- **Setup**: Emulate 2GB RAM, Snapdragon 4xx performance
- **Expected**: 45+ FPS maintained throughout
- **Bots should**: Not stutter, pathfind smoothly
- **Feel**: "Runs great even on my old phone"

### Test 6: Player Loss Fairness
- **Setup**: Player loses to a bot 1-on-1
- **Expected**: Player feels the loss was "earned" not "stolen"
- **Bots should**: Have visible moments of competence and moments of weakness
- **Feel**: "I could have won if I'd played better"

